window.docContents[173].resolve({"/Algebraic-Graph-Theory/#section-counting-copies-of-cycles":{"contents":"By labelledCopyCount_eq_copyCount_mul_labelledCopyCount, the number of labelled\ncopies of a finite graph A in a finite graph B is the number of unlabelled copies\ntimes the number of automorphisms of A. Since the automorphism group of C[n + 3]\nis the dihedral group of order 2 * (n + 3) (autCycleGraphMulEquivDihedral), this\nexpresses the number of labelled copies of a cycle in a graph in terms of the number\nof unlabelled copies.\n\ntheorem labelledCopyCount_cycleGraph [Fintype V] (G : SimpleGraph V) (n : ℕ) :\n    G.labelledCopyCount C[n + 3] = G.copyCount C[n + 3] * (2 * (n + 3)) := by\n  rw [labelledCopyCount_eq_copyCount_mul_labelledCopyCount, labelledCopyCount,\n    ← DihedralGroup.card, ← Fintype.card_congr ((copyEquivAut C[n + 3]).trans\n    (autCycleGraphMulEquivDihedral n).toEquiv)]\n  -- Both sides now have the form G.copyCount C[n + 3] * Fintype.card (Copy …),\n  -- but the Fintype instances differ: the left one comes from\n  -- labelledCopyCount, where it is built classically, and the right one from type\n  -- class search in Fintype.card_congr. rfl would have to check that they are\n  -- definitionally equal, which times out. convert closes the gap using\n  -- Subsingleton (any two Fintype instances are equal).\n  convert rfl\n\nend copies\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Algebraic Graph Theory\u0009Counting Copies*","header":"12.7.4. Counting Copies of Cycles","id":"/Algebraic-Graph-Theory/#section-counting-copies-of-cycles"}});